Hop out of the truck to meet {{ho|Mom}} and step inside your new home.

===Home===
====2F====
Head upstairs to check out your room and set the clock. After doing so, Mom tells you that the movers have finished their work, and to make sure that everything for your desk is here. The desk holds a notebook with adventure rules, and a [[PC]] in the corner.

The [[PC]] acts as your {{DL|PC|Item Storage System|item storage}}. Since each pocket on your [[Bag]] can only hold 20 different [[item]]s, it would be necessary to use or discard some before obtaining anything new. The PC can hold up to 50 different items. ''Withdraw Item'' and ''Deposit Item'' allow for moving items between inventory and storage, while ''Toss Item'' discards an item permanently. There is also a ''Mailbox'' function to store pieces of [[Mail]], as well as a ''{{DL|Decoration|Generation III decorations|Decoration}}'' option.

To save the game, press <sc>Start</sc> to open the main menu, select ''Save'', and then ''Yes''. When the menu disappears, your progress is saved and it is safe to exit the game.

====1F====
Return to the first floor and Mom excitedly calls you over to the TV, as the current program just aired a segment about the [[Petalburg Gym]], where your father is the new [[Gym Leader]]. She then suggests visiting his friend, your new neighbor, [[Professor Birch]].

===Birch's house===
Visit the house next door to meet [[Professor Birch]]'s wife, then go upstairs to meet their child, {{ga|May}}/{{ga|Brendan}}. The young Pokémon Trainer is happy to meet you, but leaves suddenly a moment later after remembering that Birch asked for help in catching a Pokémon.
