* The gecko-based Pokémon {{p|Treecko}} is the {{t|Grass}}-type starter. It's effective against the first [[Gym]], but later can prove difficult. It doesn't gain a second type upon evolution.
* The chicken-based Pokémon {{p|Torchic}} is the {{t|Fire}}-type starter. It can have trouble against the first Gym, but gains a secondary {{t|Fighting}}-type upon evolution.
* The fish Pokémon {{p|Mudkip}} is the {{t|Water}} type starter. It's effective against the first Gym and retains useful upon it. As it evolves, it gains a secondary {{t|Ground}}-type upon evolution.

Once the wild {{p|Poochyena}} is defeated, Birch invites you back to the Lab.

==Littleroot Town==
===Birch's Lab===
As thanks for rescuing him, Birch happily lets you keep the young Pokémon. He gives you a chance to [[nickname]] your [[first partner Pokémon]], then encourages you to visit {{ga|May}}/{{ga|Brendan}} on {{rt|103|Hoenn}} for tips on how to be a Pokémon Trainer. When your Pokémon needs a rest, head back home and speak to Mom at any time to have her restore it to full health.

==Oldale Town==
[[File:Oldale Town RS.png|thumb|Oldale Town]]

[[Oldale Town]] is a small town located between {{rt|101|Hoenn}} to the south, {{rt|102|Hoenn}} to the west, and {{rt|103|Hoenn}} to the north. It is where the contrast between colorful flowers and deep, verdant forests is most beautiful.

