Having witnessed your ability as a Trainer, {{ga|May}}/{{ga|Brendan}} is not surprised that [[Professor Birch]] has taken an interest in you. She/He then turns to leave, jumping down the [[ledge]]s on the way southward to Birch's lab.

==Oldale Town==
===Heading Home===
{{ga|May}}/{{ga|Brendan}} is waiting for you near [[Oldale Town]]'s south exit. When you approach, she/he excitedly sets off again toward [[Littleroot Town]].

==Littleroot Town==
===Birch's Lab===
When you return to Birch's lab, he congratulates you on defeating {{ga|May}}/{{ga|Brendan}} on your first try. He explains that his child has been helping with his research for a long time, and she/he already has an extensive history as a Trainer. Birch then reveals a device that he had ordered for his research, but decides to give to you instead: the [[Pokédex]]. This handheld device is a high-tech encyclopedia that records data on every Pokémon you encounter, and will be complete when you catch a member of every species. May/Brendan is thrilled to see you get your own Pokédex just like her/him, and gives you five {{i|Poké Ball}}s to start you on your journey.

===Run Like the Wind===
As you go to leave [[Littleroot Town]] again, {{ho|Mom}} is waiting outside for you. Realizing that you are headed out on an adventure, she suggests wearing the pair of [[Running Shoes]] that she brought for you. With these Running Shoes on, holding the B Button allows you to move at twice the speed as walking. Mom says that Dad will be overjoyed that you have your very own Pokémon, but asks that you be careful. She reminds you that you can come home to visit anytime before heading back inside, leaving you free to begin your journey.

==Oldale Town==
===“Rare” Footprints===
By the time you return to [[Oldale Town]], the west exit is no longer blocked. The Super Nerd who was sketching what he believed to be rare Pokémon footprints can be found in the center of town, and sheepishly admits that they were his own.



